hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19189","Waki narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Buhayr, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, he said: My family sent me with a milch camel to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered me to milk it. So I milked it, and he said to me: Leave the caller of the milk."
"19190","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Yaqub ibn Buhayr, a man of the clan, he said: I heard Dirar ibn al-Azwar, he said: We gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a milch camel. He said: So I milked it. He said: Then when I took to exhaust her he said: Do not do so; leave the caller of the milk."
"19191","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abd Allah ibn Sinan, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him while he milked and said: Leave the caller of the milk."
"19192","Abd Allah said: And Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to me: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, or from al-Amash, from Yaqub ibn Buhayr, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with like it."
